
# Firebase Integration Rules

Agent-requested attachment - use when working with Firebase code.

## Modular SDK Usage
Always use the v9+ modular SDK, never the compat or v8 SDK.

```tsx
// ✅ Correct - Modular SDK
import { getAuth, signInWithPopup, GoogleAuthProvider } from 'firebase/auth';
import { getFirestore, collection, doc, getDocs } from 'firebase/firestore';
import { getStorage, ref, uploadBytes } from 'firebase/storage';

// ❌ Wrong - Compat SDK
import firebase from 'firebase/compat/app';
```

## Environment Variables
- Store config in `.env.local` (never commit to git)
- Use `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix for client-side vars only when necessary
- Server-side config should not be exposed to client

```
# .env.local
FIREBASE_API_KEY=your_api_key
FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your_project.firebaseapp.com
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your_project_id
```

## Security Rules
- Never expose Firebase config keys in client code
- Use Firebase Security Rules for data access control
- Validate all data on both client and server
- Use `zod` schemas for runtime validation

## Data Patterns
```tsx
// Firestore queries
const episodesRef = collection(db, 'episodes');
const q = query(
  episodesRef, 
  where('seriesId', '==', seriesId),
  orderBy('createdAt', 'desc'),
  limit(10)
);

// Error handling
try {
  const snapshot = await getDocs(q);
  const episodes = snapshot.docs.map(doc => ({
    id: doc.id,
    ...doc.data()
  }));
} catch (error) {
  console.error('Firestore error:', error);
  throw new Error('Failed to fetch episodes');
}
```

